# QR Code Generator — a Skia QR code (gradient fill + DiscretePathEffect) that is
# regenerated from a TextInput (empty input falls back to "reactiive.io"), plus a
# custom gesture-handler "Deviation" slider driving the path-effect deviation on
# the UI thread.
# What this test covers: typing a URL, typing unicode/CJK/emoji (multi-byte QR
# payload), clearing the input with backspace (fallback value), dismissing the
# keyboard by tapping the content, dragging the slider to 0 and to max, dragging
# far past both ends (clamp), a slow scrub, quick repeated grabs of the thumb.
# NOTE: pasting >1273 bytes (QR level H capacity) throws "The amount of data is
# too big to be stored in a QR Code" as a Render Error — not reproducible here
# because typing that much text through XCTest is too slow; see report.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/qr-code-generator"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait "text" "Deviation" 10000
wait 1000
press 201 140
wait 800
type "https://reactiive.io/demos"
wait 1000
# Tap the QR (TouchableWithoutFeedback -> Keyboard.dismiss).
press 201 360
wait 1000
# Slider thumb starts at x=201 (track 25..377, y=661).
gesture pan 201 661 -176 0 600
wait 800
gesture pan 25 661 352 0 800
wait 800
# Past both ends: translateX must clamp.
gesture pan 377 661 -370 0 300
wait 600
gesture pan 25 661 370 0 300
wait 600
# Slow scrub back to the middle.
gesture pan 377 661 -176 0 2500
wait 800
# Quick repeated grabs (onBegin springs border/scale each time).
press 201 661 --count 4 --interval-ms 150
wait 800
# Clear the input with backspace (fallback "reactiive.io" QR), then unicode.
press 201 140
wait 800
press 372 720 --count 30 --interval-ms 20
wait 800
type "Ünïcødé ✓ 漢字 🚀"
wait 1000
press 201 360
wait 1000
gesture pan 201 661 120 0 500
wait 1000
wait "text" "Deviation" 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
